title: "Supply chain resilience under stochastic disruptions: graph-flow model and computational framework"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible computational framework for assessing the structural and functional
  resilience of supply chain networks under stochastic disruptions. The network is a
  directed capacitated graph; functionality is the normalized maximum flow from a
  supersource to a supersink; resilience is evaluated over a performance trajectory by
  an integral index, robustness, final recovery level and a lower-tail (CVaR) risk
  metric under a Monte Carlo protocol.
